 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "microwave not working"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "A microwave that appears completely dead usually points to a simple power issue first. Please check that the plug is securely inserted and try using a different appliance on that socket to rule out a tripped fuse or switched-off outlet. If the socket works, let me know if the display lights up at all when you press any buttons."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "the display is on, shows the time. it beeps when I press buttons but won't start"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Since the display is on and beeping but won't start, this usually points to a settings issue rather than a power fault. First, check if your microwave has a control or child lock active (often shown by a key or lock symbol). Try holding 'Stop' for 3 seconds to see if it unlocks. If that doesn't work, please try putting a cup of water in and pressing Start for one minute on full power."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "there's a little L symbol on the display. holding Stop for 3 secs made it go away and now it works"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That’s excellent news. The 'L' symbol suggests the child lock was active, which is a common safety feature to prevent accidental operation. To avoid this happening again, just remember that holding the Stop button for a few seconds will toggle the lock on and off whenever you need it. If you have any other questions or if anything else comes up with your appliances, feel free to ask."
  }
 ],
